direction: down

title: |md
  ### Inbound TCP demux: full identity first, listeners second
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

pkt: "tcp_v4_rcv: validated TCP segment" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  p_body: |md
    Header supplies peer/local addresses + ports.

    `__inet_lookup_skb()` may first reuse a
    prefetched skb socket; otherwise it calls
    `__inet_lookup()` with namespace and
    ingress-device identity.
  |
}

ehash: "Tier 1: ehash full-identity lookup" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  e_body: |md
    `__inet_lookup_established()`

    hash(netns, daddr, dport, saddr, sport)
      → one ehash bucket

    RCU nulls-list walk + exact revalidation:
    namespace, address/port pair, interfaces

    Hit takes a refcount and can be:
    - full TCP socket
    - TCP_TIME_WAIT minisock
    - TCP_NEW_SYN_RECV request sock
  |
}

special: "Dispatch by returned socket state" {
  style.fill: "#ede9fe"
  s_body: |md
    TIME_WAIT
      → tcp_timewait_state_process (Day 15)

    NEW_SYN_RECV
      → listener/request completion path

    LISTEN or full connection
      → policy/filter + tcp_v4_do_rcv
         (or full-socket backlog if user-owned)
  |
}

listener: "Tier 2: listener lookup after ehash miss" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  l_body: |md
    1. Optional BPF SK_LOOKUP redirect
    2. lhash2(netns, daddr, dport)
       score specific-address candidates
    3. lhash2(netns, INADDR_ANY, dport)
       score wildcard listeners

    `ipv4_portaddr_hash`, not the 4-tuple hash.
    SO_REUSEPORT selection occurs within a
    candidate group; lhash2 serves all listeners.

    A miss is not proof the packet was a SYN.
  |
}

miss: "No matching full-identity entry or listener" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  m_body: |md
    Set `SKB_DROP_REASON_NO_SOCKET`.

    After policy and checksum validation,
    send a reset when the segment permits one;
    then release the skb.

    A connect attempt sees that RST as
    ECONNREFUSED, but stray packets use this path too.
  |
}

namespace: "Where the tables live" {
  style.fill: "#fff7ed"
  n_body: |md
    Lookup is always namespace-aware.

    Child netns may request a private ehash via
    `tcp_child_ehash_entries`; otherwise it uses
    shared global hash storage with netns in
    hash/match identity.
  |
}

pkt -> ehash: "lookup full identity"
ehash -> special: "hit + held reference"
ehash -> listener: "miss"
listener -> special: "listener selected"
listener -> miss: "no candidate"
namespace -> ehash: "select hashinfo + namespace identity" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
namespace -> listener: "namespace participates in lookup" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
